  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 128 PM CDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nA potent 594 dm ridge shifts east over the area today through \nMonday. Drier air is mixing down this afternoon and bringing our\ndewpoints down into the lower 60s and even a few upper 50s. Sfc\nhigh pressure will build to our east tomorrow and bring \nsoutherly/southwesterly return flow. Even with the increase in \nmoisture transport, dewpoints will still be in the 60s tomorrow.\nThis will allow for highs to climb into the lower to mid 90s. \n\nNext week continues to look hot with heat indices reaching 100+ \ndegrees as early as Monday out west in the NBM. The LREF starts to \nincrease the probabilities of 100+ degree heat indices on Monday \nwith a 20-40% chance and jumps up to a 60-80% chance on Tuesday, and \na 70-90% chance on Wednesday and Thursday. While a few sites \nmight hit a heat index of 105 (Heat Advisory criteria), a Heat \nAdvisory will still be necessary due to there being 4 \nconsecutive days of heat indices of 100+. \n\nThe ridge aloft begins to flatten on Thursday and then shifts west \non Friday and Saturday. Friday and Saturday may still be hot though \nwith highs potentially in the mid 90s and LREF probs of 50-70% of \nheat indices of 100+ on Friday, and 40-60% on Saturday. Some \nweak, scattered 20%ish PoPs re-enter the forecast late week into\nthe weekend as a few ripples move through the ridge and a cold \nfront stalls to the north. However, ensembles are slightly more \nrobust with precip chances during that time frame, which could \nbring a little more (albeit still limited) relief from the heat.",
